cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MassJ.jl
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexandre
    family-names: Giuliani
    email: giuliani@synchrotron-soleil.fr
    affiliation: Synchrotron SOLEIL
repository-code: "https://github.com/ajgiuliani/MassJ.jl"
url: "https://ajgiuliani.github.io/MassJ.jl/stable"
abstract: >-
  MassJ.jl is a Julia package for loading, processing, and analysing mass
  spectrometry data. It supports the common open file formats (mzML, mzXML,
  MGF, MSP, imzML), provides signal-processing tools (Savitzky-Golay smoothing,
  centroiding, baseline correction), isotopic distribution calculations,
  UniDec-style charge-state deconvolution, energy-resolved peak yields with
  per-scan error propagation, and Plots.jl recipes for native plotting.
keywords:
  - mass spectrometry
  - mzML
  - mzXML
  - proteomics
  - isotopic distribution
  - charge deconvolution
  - julia
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
